<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Turkey nominates former foreign minister Sinirlioglu as UN chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30b7b0cfb79858b27361a99113a84f2ea9efcb5cd76bd88686f53bebd97d3817</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:37:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T14:28:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261031-turkey-nominates-former-foreign-minister-sinirlioglu-as-un-chief--8c6274edaf1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261031-turkey-nominates-former-foreign-minister-sinirlioglu-as-un-chief" /><summary type="html">Turkey has nominated its former foreign minister and UN ambassador Feridun Hadi Sinirlioglu for the position of UN secretary-general, state-media reported on Saturday. The submission was officially backed by Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan who has been particularly vocal in calling for reform of the UN Security Council.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Binance hit by 6.3 billion dollar crypto theft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ded1786a89d30a48d9ef6497edee2abb7fe7754f5eae5bf59b07a50b5bcd32d</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:37:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T11:16:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/binance-hit-by-6-3-billion-dollar-crypto-theft--c6fff32fd669.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/binance-hit-by-6-3-billion-dollar-crypto-theft" /><summary type="html">Binance executives are scrambling to recover billions of dollars after the crypto platform was hit by what is being described as the biggest heist in cryptocurrency history. Hackers reportedly stole $6.3 billion from users, with analysts pointing the finger at North Korea. The attack far surpasses the previous record set in February 2025, when hackers stole $1.5 billion from crypto exchange Bybit.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's Nunez warns of high risk during protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8464796bdf605ddc38267438e7f356d6045e8a6a9c497aa5c92852b20ae6bb13</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:37:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T11:15:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-nunez-warns-of-high-risk-during-protests--a28190b09542.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-nunez-warns-of-high-risk-during-protests" /><summary type="html">France is bracing for a third consecutive weekend of protests, with around 70,000 security personnel deployed to prevent a repeat of the violence seen on October 17. Shops have boarded up their premises as authorities warn of further clashes, with Halloween celebrations adding to security concerns over masked demonstrators. The protests, involving Yellow Vest activists, trade unions and students, initially focused on the rising cost of living, inequality and poor school conditions, but have since expanded to include demands for greater civil liberties and the right to protest. The demonstrations come six months ahead of presidential elections, amid a tense political climate and growing support for the far right. Authorities have restricted marches in several cities, while Paris police have only authorised a demonstration on the capital's outskirts. Curfews have also been imposed in parts of Paris as officials seek to prevent further unrest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Third weekend of protests in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f1a660500d231e9dc6b394f4a89b2fdf8135fde180f3b80381bd2c098681228</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:37:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T11:13:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/third-weekend-of-protests-in-france--55e916671654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/third-weekend-of-protests-in-france" /><summary type="html">France is preparing for a third weekend of protests, with 70,000 security personnel deployed to prevent a repeat of the violence seen on October 17. Shops have boarded up their premises as authorities warn of further clashes, with Halloween adding to concerns over masked demonstrators. The protests, initially driven by anger over the cost of living and poor school conditions, have broadened to include demands for greater civil liberties and the right to protest. With presidential elections six months away, authorities have tightened security and restricted demonstrations in several cities.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump vs MAGA: Why his movement is splitting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3bca5ad8785e2711f6dc1f108b8a4e67be2b7d844aeded89f73bb788bc12f2f9</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:37:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T10:11:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261031-trump-vs-maga-why-his-movement-is-splitting--4267dc0a4776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261031-trump-vs-maga-why-his-movement-is-splitting" /><summary type="html">As the 2026 midterm elections approach, divisions within the MAGA camp are becoming increasingly visible. From the war in Iran and rising fuel prices to the Epstein files, several of Trump’s decisions are fuelling divisions among his most loyal supporters.
 
Once united by a shared vision of America, MAGA now brings together factions that increasingly disagree over foreign policy, the economy and what “America First” should actually mean. Yet Trump remains the central figure holding this political coalition together – and he is fighting to keep it that way.
 
Why are some of the president’s longtime allies distancing themselves from him? Can MAGA remain united despite these disagreements? And can Trump still mobilise his base ahead of the midterms?
 
🔍 Our journalist Stella Elgersma breaks down the divisions within the MAGA movement and Donald Trump’s strategy to rally his supporters, once again.</summary></entry><entry><title>PSG secure 9th consecutive win thanks to Achraf Hakimi hat-trick</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f22f701e77f8ae95a81cb71d8980aabe4e386b4660acccb854169871c37fc23</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:37:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:51:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261031-psg-secure-9th-consecutive-win-thanks-to-achraf-hakimi-hat-trick--1903af1e9ac9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261031-psg-secure-9th-consecutive-win-thanks-to-achraf-hakimi-hat-trick" /><summary type="html">A night to remember for PSG in Le Havre. In the opening fixture of Ligue 1's ninth round, the French champions thrashed Le Havre at the Stade Océane, inspired by an outstanding performance from Achraf Hakimi. The Moroccan star scored a hat-trick and provided two assists, playing a decisive role in all five of his team's goals. PSG strengthened their grip on top spot, while Le Havre remain rooted to the bottom of the table.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>'Atmosphere of fear': Trump moves to curtail voting rights ahead of the midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fb849bba681cb86a56c205e55c6d78316e5a046c8277209ec9dfb339d1e804a</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:40:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-united-states-atmosphere-of-fear-trump-moves-to-curtail-voting-rights-ahead-of-the-midterms--ef0cd17927a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-united-states-atmosphere-of-fear-trump-moves-to-curtail-voting-rights-ahead-of-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">Americans vote on November 3 in midterm elections that could see Republicans lose control of Congress, endangering US President Donald Trump's legislative agenda. Under the US Constitution, elections are organized by the respective states – but that has not halted US President Donald Trump from trying to wield his influence ahead of the vote.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal hosts Africa’s first ever Youth Olympic Games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efc42be9e9998de037fb526b21f4da52851455d1c302f70c52add3cc4cff689f</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:37:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261031-senegal-hosts-africa-s-first-ever-youth-olympic-games--48359a071e4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261031-senegal-hosts-africa-s-first-ever-youth-olympic-games" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Youth Olympic Games opens with a spectacular ceremony Saturday in the Senegalese capital Dakar in the first ever Olympics to be held on African soil. It comes as the continent seeks a bigger role in international sporting competitions.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Protesters gather at Poland's Top court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65bca28931377c5b69c2f2f3730a446515df5d1a47ca1c3734384d1649fc756f</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:31:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/protesters-gather-at-poland-s-top-court--ffa4a59e5a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/protesters-gather-at-poland-s-top-court" /><summary type="html">Police in Poland have stepped up security around the country’s Constitutional Tribunal after dozens of protesters gathered on Friday to oppose the government’s suspension of its president, which they say was unlawful. Police say several people were detained after some demonstrators breached the court’s perimeter fence. Charlotte Hughes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's presence divides G20 ministers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc47c74583019c50e73146e1cb6d099e176c2dc94623861da24b42423bc54c4a</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:30:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-presence-divides-g20-ministers--30d63f369093.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-presence-divides-g20-ministers" /><summary type="html">The G20 foreign ministers’ meeting in the US is wrapping up two days of talks without agreement on several key global security issues. On the sidelines, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio signed an Arctic cooperation deal with Japan and South Korea and confirmed Washington’s participation in Riyadh’s World Expo in 2030. Meanwhile, European ministers confronted Russia’s Sergei Lavrov over the war in Ukraine and refused to join him for the traditional group photo. Jack Pownall reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>French Interior Minister fears disorder after dark on Halloween</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b29014fb42b8da7cc736c7f56fbb631589002e436bce5b27a5be8924b84f12c2</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:28:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-interior-minister-fears-disorder-after-dark-on-halloween--5af5a8eb794e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-interior-minister-fears-disorder-after-dark-on-halloween" /><summary type="html">Saturday is set to see another day of nationwide demonstrations over the cost of living and conditions in schools. Dubbed “Act Three”, the protests bring together Yellow Vest activists and student demonstrators. But France’s highest administrative court has just upheld a ban on the planned route of the Paris march, forcing protesters to remain on the eastern outskirts of the capital. Authorities are deploying 70,000 security personnel and imposing curfews in some areas, repeating many of the measures seen last weekend. The interior minister has also issued a Halloween-themed warning: covering your face at a demonstration remains illegal. Ophelie Jacobson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Two rallies against racism near Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82acded620ee3c5657bb5a3b6e742062f52b98e00b05fa6af9c3a9bcc4f0f576</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:27:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-two-rallies-against-racism-near-paris--7254a265916b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-two-rallies-against-racism-near-paris" /><summary type="html">France is bracing for a third weekend of protests, with demonstrations against the rising cost of living planned across the country. Nearly half a million people are expected to take to the streets, prompting the government to deploy 70,000 police officers to maintain order. In Paris, a last-minute court ruling has restricted today’s march to the eastern outskirts of the capital. Jack Pownall reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>France braces for Halloween protests, shops board up storefronts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e64247479def9e1d6d5aaee417f13a549363eaa061d78bf1f7542098d03ce6e</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T07:40:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-halloween-protests-shops-board-up-storefronts--e0ba7b06e2ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-halloween-protests-shops-board-up-storefronts" /><summary type="html">France on Saturday braced for a third weekend of protests coinciding with Halloween, as shops boarded up and authorities scrambled to prevent a repeat of the street violence that swept the country two weeks ago.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro posts video, says he fled Brazil due to ‘persecution’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbd8224d65e17560219599684fec7136dc0f80e4c2856b736c56069c94ff6d39</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T06:25:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-flavio-bolsonaro-posts-video-says-he-fled-brazil-due-to-persecution--3ad01377532f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-flavio-bolsonaro-posts-video-says-he-fled-brazil-due-to-persecution" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro posted a video message on social media late Friday to declare he had fled to the US because he was a victim of 'persecution'. Bolsonaro, who lost Sunday's election runoff to President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, gave no details of how he left the country.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Some 15,000 demonstrators taking part in protests across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bec180ccf3c4f84d2067462092db56909c452470a55c9e8478de19f67556ad05</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T05:53:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261031-live-france-braces-for-halloween-protests-government-vows-tough-response--6825697d0a22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261031-live-france-braces-for-halloween-protests-government-vows-tough-response" /><summary type="html">Around 15,000 protesters were taking part in demonstrations across France on Saturday, according to the interior ministry, as the country braced for a third weekend of protests which Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez deemed as “high risk”. Around 70,000 security personnel were deployed, as authorities sought to avert a repeat of the unrest that swept the country two weeks ago. Follow our live blog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Halloween Protests &amp; French Promises, US Mid Term Mood, What now for Israel?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:821119654f1db4ffa993a6b89d735e98bd7014f594d84bdd930a458a71ae25ad</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T00:30:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261031-halloween-protests-french-promises-us-mid-term-mood-what-now-for-israel--7b34e314fd8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261031-halloween-protests-french-promises-us-mid-term-mood-what-now-for-israel" /><summary type="html">France braces for another weekend of unrest as the Yellow Vests return to the streets under the rallying cry of ‘Act III – Halloween’, with 70,000 police and security forces deployed after the riots and looting of recent weeks. A cash-strapped government faces mounting grievances, a rolling protest movement and little room for manoeuvre ahead of elections, as it struggles to restore order while grappling with crippling debt.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Trump admin approves potential Patriot missiles sale to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b65c4e0d126c839e229bff6499999d1a984a6cd484c8cc286d2da27727669755</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T23:19:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-trump-admin-approves-potential-patriot-missiles-sale-to-ukraine--23216ec77f01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-trump-admin-approves-potential-patriot-missiles-sale-to-ukraine" /><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>First Youth Olympic Games in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6900473b0446dfbc24057add7321a4b9d7a15c1452201bd38a730ee6e4199bdd</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T21:48:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/first-youth-olympic-games-in-africa--c6de06960cd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/first-youth-olympic-games-in-africa" /><summary type="html">In tonight's show, the Senegalese capital is hosting the first Olympic event ever held in Africa, welcoming nearly 2,700 athletes for the 2026 Youth Olympic Games. Also, South Africa’s local elections are set for November 4, with the African National Congress facing growing pressure over its record in local government. And finally we are joined by Muse L'Artiste who's reconnecting to her roots with her latest EP Heritage bringing her father's compositions back to life.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Residents leave Russian-occupied Oleshky in evacuation operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c5ed37e6a262e16c1cf18af40e592526a8c1a1023c852ed5591cf91ea62ec75</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T21:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-residents-leave-russian-occupied-oleshky-in-evacuation-operation--14ad8cd95743.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-residents-leave-russian-occupied-oleshky-in-evacuation-operation" /><summary type="html">Residents evacuated from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky have left for Russia's Anapa city with a Ukrainian delegation, senior official David Arakhamia said Friday. They are expected to fly to Belarus before returning to Ukraine by bus, during a rare ceasefire brokered by the United States.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UN nature summit approves two key agreements after marathon negotiations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba945a84bf9cc9bb3ba37b27e18360d30cfaf1a9f88f4c715b6f3c1e88912f49</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T20:52:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20261030-un-nature-summit-approves-two-key-agreements-after-marathon-negotiations--0393797d624e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261030-un-nature-summit-approves-two-key-agreements-after-marathon-negotiations" /><summary type="html">Almost 200 nations approved two agreements on Friday to halt biodiversity loss by 2030, following almost two weeks of negotiations that ran into extra time on the final day.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>'Five churches set on fire by Muslims?' Fake news by Islamophobic social media accounts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:120cb35630da54c0b68ffd3df029b884f5b653234c0de9ac0c1ee77f91fe8787</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T18:37:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261030-five-churches-set-on-fire-by-muslims-fake-news-from-islamophobic-social-media-accounts--b8bc106a3649.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261030-five-churches-set-on-fire-by-muslims-fake-news-from-islamophobic-social-media-accounts" /><summary type="html">Several social media accounts associated with sharing anti-immigrant views claim French Muslims were responsible for burning five churches on October 17 – the day the nation was rocked by en masse protests. But both this number and story are fictitious. The French government agency that monitors religious heritage sites confirmed only one fire in a church occured in recent days; its cause unknown.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>MAGA: Why Trump's movement is fracturing?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64db4bb462e507cf938eb121854f65181556d4eee70a1e0217390a5aab2fb2d1</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T18:01:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-maga-why-trump-s-movement-is-fracturing--e5d6b934be9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-maga-why-trump-s-movement-is-fracturing" /><summary type="html">As the 2026 midterm elections approach, divisions within the MAGA camp are becoming increasingly visible. From the war in Iran and rising fuel prices to the Epstein files, several of Trump’s decisions are fuelling divisions among his most loyal supporters.
 
Once united by a shared vision of America, MAGA now brings together factions that increasingly disagree over foreign policy, the economy and what “America First” should actually mean. Yet Trump remains the central figure holding this political coalition together – and he is fighting to keep it that way.
 
Why are some of the president’s longtime allies distancing themselves from him? Can MAGA remain united despite these disagreements? And can Trump still mobilise his base ahead of the midterms?
 
🔍 Our journalist Stella Elgersma breaks down the divisions within the MAGA movement and Donald Trump’s strategy to rally his supporters, once again.</summary></entry><entry><title>Oleshky: No access to basic needs, ceasefire offers limited opportunity for humanitarian assistance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff8d247a5015cf7425a82f9d821136249b638d7a2c99c0d2b3a5d06777fefedb</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T17:11:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/oleshky-no-access-to-basic-needs-ceasefire-offers-limited-opportunity-for-humanitarian-assistance--31d5d457bf7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/oleshky-no-access-to-basic-needs-ceasefire-offers-limited-opportunity-for-humanitarian-assistance" /><summary type="html">Catherine Viette is pleased to welcome Jens Schumacher, Field Coordinator in Mykolaiv and Kherson with Solidarity International. Just a few kilometers separate the Ukrainian-controlled city of Kherson from Russian-occupied Oleshky. For civilians caught between military occupation, disrupted essential services and uncertain evacuation arrangements, geographical proximity offers little guarantee of access to life-saving assistance. Schumacher examines the humanitarian implications of a temporary ceasefire around Oleshky, where approximately 2,000 civilians were reported to remain. Although the cessation of attacks has created a limited opportunity for humanitarian operations, the geographical scope of the agreement, the prospects for evacuation and the possibility of sustained humanitarian access remain uncertain.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia’s Novaya Gazeta to cease publication amid Kremlin crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3571f798d04a3b46328302beedff86bd073d5e78c93711a4029f8ec54885ca5</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:38:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:58:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-russia-s-novaya-gazeta-to-cease-publication-amid-kremlin-crackdown--16d905f32e82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-russia-s-novaya-gazeta-to-cease-publication-amid-kremlin-crackdown" /><summary type="html">Russia’s most renowned independent newspaper, Novaya Gazeta, announced on Friday that it was ceasing publication after more than three decades. Known for its courageous investigative journalism, the flagship newspaper said the Kremlin’s crackdown and ban on the media outlet had made it impossible to continue its work.</summary></entry></feed>
